@startuml 05-seq-expiry
title Expiry job: at startup and on the configured cron (US-202, US-203, US-204)

autonumber
participant "Spring\n(ApplicationReadyEvent / @Scheduled cron)" as Spring
participant ExpiryScheduler
participant ExpiryService
participant Clock
participant TradeRepository
participant AuditEventFactory
participant OutboxRepository
database PostgreSQL

alt application started (US-203: catch up after downtime)
  Spring -> ExpiryScheduler : onApplicationReady()
else cron fires (default "0 5 0 * * *" in the configured zone: US-202.4)
  Spring -> ExpiryScheduler : runScheduled()
end
ExpiryScheduler -> ExpiryService : expireMaturedTrades()
ExpiryService -> Clock : today = LocalDate.now(clock)
ExpiryService -> PostgreSQL : BEGIN
ExpiryService -> TradeRepository : markExpired(today)
TradeRepository -> PostgreSQL : UPDATE trades SET expired = true\nWHERE maturity_date < ? AND expired = false\nRETURNING *
note right of PostgreSQL
  "<" not "<=": a trade maturing today stays live (A-17).
  Already-expired rows are never returned, so a re-run
  writes nothing (idempotent, US-202.2). The job never
  sets expired back to false (US-204.2).
end note
TradeRepository --> ExpiryService : List<Trade> (newly expired)
loop each newly expired trade
  ExpiryService -> AuditEventFactory : expired(trade)  (channel = SCHEDULER)
  ExpiryService -> OutboxRepository : append(EXPIRED event)
end
ExpiryService -> PostgreSQL : COMMIT
ExpiryService --> ExpiryScheduler : count
ExpiryScheduler -> ExpiryScheduler : log INFO "expired {count} trades"

alt PostgreSQL unavailable
  PostgreSQL --> ExpiryService : DataAccessException
  ExpiryService --> ExpiryScheduler : rethrow
  ExpiryScheduler -> ExpiryScheduler : log ERROR; the next run (or restart) catches up
end

note over ExpiryScheduler, PostgreSQL
  Several instances may run the job at once: the UPDATE row locks
  make each trade expire (and be audited) exactly once (A-42).
end note

@enduml
